# fixedbugs, defect 2877, 2026-11-27, lane win-longname (M-rebel-library step
# 212e).
#
# SYMPTOM: the shape beside the run case's: two modules whose names take 180
# letters and share all but the last each bind an inline body of
# `fixedbugs-2877-inline.h` that calls `base2877`, which nothing on the link
# line defines. On Windows the program did not compile from the CI's
# checkout, *the operating system's own reason is 3* at a unit's file, exit 2,
# before the link could refuse anything.
#
# FIX: a unit's files are named by the module's stem
# (`selfhost/cli/unit_names.hero`), and the link's refusal, which names an
# object by its file alone under ld64 and MSVC's `link.exe`, is placed at the
# module whose stem the object opens with (`cli/needs_placed.hero`): each
# module told at its own binding, as defect 2495's case tells two modules
# with short names. A name cut at a length would have left the two one name.
use fixedbugs2877/amodulewhoseobjectisnamedbyadigestofitsnameistoldatitsownbindingwhenalinkrefusesanameitsheadersinlinebodiescallandsoisanothermodulewhosenamesharesallbutitslastletterwithitsownnamea as first
use fixedbugs2877/amodulewhoseobjectisnamedbyadigestofitsnameistoldatitsownbindingwhenalinkrefusesanameitsheadersinlinebodiescallandsoisanothermodulewhosenamesharesallbutitslastletterwithitsownnameb as second

function main()
    print(first.a() + second.b())
